    "findings": [
      {
        "file": "nbd/server.c",
        "start_line": 2455,
        "end_line": 2455,
        "side": "new",
        "severity": "high",
        "category": "security",
        "title": "Client-reachable assert when no meta context was set for the export",
        "explanation": "client->contexts.exp is only assigned during NBD_OPT_SET_META_CONTEXT; nbd_check_meta_export merely zeroes count on mismatch and never syncs exp. An extended-mode client that skips SET_META_CONTEXT (or sets it for a different export before GO) and then sends NBD_CMD_BLOCK_STATUS with NBD_CMD_FLAG_PAYLOAD_LEN reaches this function with contexts.exp == NULL (or another export) != client->exp, aborting the server via assert(). The BLOCK_STAT_PAYLOAD export flag is advertised only when contexts.count != 0, but nothing in this function prevents a noncompliant client from sending the flag anyway. Unless the caller (hunk #4, not visible here) gates this call on client->contexts.count, this is a remote DoS.",
        "suggestion": "Replace the assert with a graceful check: if client->contexts.count == 0 || client->contexts.exp != client->exp, set request->len = request->contexts->count = 0 and drop payload_len bytes (the skip path), so the request fails with NBD_EINVAL instead of aborting; or ensure the caller only invokes this when contexts.count is non-zero.",
        "evidence": "    assert(client->contexts.exp == client->exp);",
        "confidence": 0.45,
        "id": "c23d1aa6f96b",
        "hunk_id": "nbd/server.c#3",
        "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
        "tier": 3,
        "escalated_from": [],
        "also_reported_by": []
      }
